Tasks for Heroes.  If you think something is missing here,
please send a note to <heroes-discuss@lists.sourceforge.net>.


Before 0.7
----------

  Write a common.h file for all macros used for portability.

  Get rid of GETWORD, SETWORD and Cie, see src/endian.h.

  Try to fix the tunnel bug on Solaris.

  Try to fix the initialization crash on Linux/m68k

  Adapt the game to allow a clean exit at any time.

  Handle SDL_quit events.

  va_dcl may be used undeclared in debugmsg.c, this is wrong.

  JUSTIF_CALC in draw.c sometimes use tricky empty parameters, this do
  no work on VC6.0.

  Check for <unistd.h> and include that file conditionnaly where 
  it is used.

  Rewrite the extras.c code to use opendir/readdir/closedir, do not
  depend on scandir.

  Use FindFileFirst and Cie. in Windows.

  Rewrite srccasecmp() for lib/.

  Check and use <stdint.h>.

  userdir.c should include string.h.

  Rewrite sleep() for lib/.

  Check for S_ISDIR, what should be done if absent?


Before 1.0.0
------------

  There are several comments in French.  They should be translated.

  Write a clean 

  The code is VERY UGLY and needs to be cleaned up.

  Split heroes.c

  Split hedlite.c

  Think of the case were two heroes process access a global score file.

  Save games/options/scores files in text format.

  Add ./configure options to configure data paths.

  Use gettext.


Left for a 1.1.x development branch
-----------------------------------

  Direct X11 support would be nice.

  The external editor should be ported too, it will need more work.

  Programmable vehicles (for CPU controled ones) would be nice.  It
  would be fun to link with Guile and control the vehicles in scheme.

  Network support.        


Miscellaneous
-------------

  What is the effect of removing the DMODE_SOFT_MUSIC from MikMod options ?

  Would Hermes be faster than LibGGI's crossblit ?

  Redesign the way menus are handled internaly.

  Write assembly routines for stretching code.

